  "question": "On one Mac, is a large TypeScript test suite faster on macOS itself, in a boxery (Lima) Linux VM, or in Docker, and how much does the VM's size matter?",
  "answer": "Every Linux VM beat macOS: 78–86 s against 112 s. Size barely mattered: 2 CPUs were within 6 s of 8. At matched sizes boxery's Lima VMs were 2–4 s faster than Docker.",
  "subject": {
    "name": "hunk",
    "repo": "https://github.com/modem-dev/hunk",
    "commit": "503efd5aa664e78241139ee9f02ae7942e811d95",
    "patch": "hunk-test-isolation.patch",
    "command": "bun run test",
    "env": {
      "HUNK_TEST_SHARDS": "2"
    },
    "tests": 5211,
    "notes": "bun run test runs scripts/test/run-test-suite.ts, which splits the suite into 2 parallel bun test processes on Linux and runs 1 on macOS unless HUNK_TEST_SHARDS is set. We pinned 2 shards everywhere for the main comparison. The patch points the tests at empty XDG config and state dirs and resolves macOS's /var symlink in 3 tests. It only changes tests."
  },
